  "id": "DrugBank_DB01234 - MONDO_6570",
  "verbalization": "Dexamethasone is implicated in the pathogenesis of Lichen Disease through a mechanism involving corticosteroid-induced immune modulation. The evidence suggests that Dexamethasone, through its indication of Exanthem, Chronic Beryllium Disease, and Erythema Multiforme, is linked to Triamcinolone, which in turn is associated with Lichen Disease. These relationships are supported by the shared use of corticosteroids in the treatment of inflammatory conditions, suggesting a potential role in immune-mediated pathophysiology. The presence of multiple corticosteroid-indicated diseases that ultimately converge on Lichen Disease highlights a possible pathway where corticosteroids modulate immune responses, potentially leading to the development of Lichen Disease. The integration of these pathways underscores the importance of corticosteroids in the management of inflammatory and autoimmune conditions, with Lichen Disease possibly being a manifestation of such immune dysregulation.",
